{"text": " Staying at home too much is quietly ruining your life. It makes your world smaller and it feeds your anxiety. When you stay at home for days, even small things begin to feel heavy. A simple trip outside to the store or the bank starts to feel like a great effort. This is not because you are weak. It is because the body forgets movement when it does not meet the world. When you remain at home, your world becomes smaller because you are living inside smaller walls. The mind grows louder in closed air, thoughts begin to circle, fear finds more space to grow. Then you step outside, you walk beneath the open sky, your eyes meet distance again and something in you opens, the breath deepens, the chest softens. The path feels wider than your worries. Even a short walk is enough to remind the heart that life is larger than one room. Step outside today, not to escape your thoughts, but to let them breathe.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 3.8, "text": " Staying at home too much is quietly ruining your life.", "tokens": [50364, 8691, 278, 412, 1280, 886, 709, 307, 19141, 38938, 428, 993, 13, 50570], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1665077109085886, "compression_ratio": 1.6228070175438596, "no_speech_prob": 0.051879532635211945, "words": [{"word": " Staying", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.6, "probability": 0.7380548715591431}, {"word": " at", "start": 0.6, "end": 0.72, "probability": 0.9941430687904358}, {"word": " home", "start": 0.72, "end": 0.88, "probability": 0.999329686164856}, {"word": " too", "start": 0.88, "end": 1.14, "probability": 0.9836967587471008}, {"word": " much", "start": 1.14, "end": 1.52, "probability": 0.9986353516578674}, {"word": " is", "start": 1.52, "end": 1.9, "probability": 0.9550394415855408}, {"word": " quietly", "start": 1.9, "end": 2.52, "probability": 0.953082263469696}, {"word": " ruining", "start": 2.52, "end": 3.0, "probability": 0.9884082674980164}, {"word": " your", "start": 3.0, "end": 3.3, "probability": 0